==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|incident|al|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɪnsɪˈdɛntəl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Loosely associated; existing as a [[byproduct]], [[tangent]], or [[accident]]; being a likely [[consequence]].
#: ''That character, though colorful, is '''incidental''' to the overall plot.''
# Occurring by chance
# (physics) Entering or approaching, prior to [[reflection]] (more frequently [[incident]]).

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|incident}}
* {{l|en|incidence}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|incidental expense}}
* {{l|en|incidentally}}
* {{l|en|incidental music}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|existing as an accident}} {{l|en|accidental}}, {{l|en|contingent}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|existing as an accident}} {{l|en|inevitable}}, {{l|en|necessary}}, {{l|en|impossible}}

